1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,634
This is Strike, by Prashant Thakur:

2
00:00:02,684 --> 00:00:06,047
weekly options vaults for
Robinhood Chain stock tokens,

3
00:00:06,097 --> 00:00:09,681
run by AI agents the
contract holds to a mandate.

4
00:00:09,831 --> 00:00:13,296
A stock token earns nothing
extra while it sits in a wallet.

5
00:00:13,346 --> 00:00:17,143
On Wall Street, holders
sell covered calls for that.

6
00:00:17,293 --> 00:00:19,259
Stock tokens also have traps:

7
00:00:19,309 --> 00:00:21,985
a multiplier that is easy to apply twice,

8
00:00:22,035 --> 00:00:25,307
weekend price freezes,
and two pause layers.

9
00:00:25,357 --> 00:00:28,189
Strike's contracts handle each one.

10
00:00:28,339 --> 00:00:32,140
Robinhood Chain, an Arbitrum
chain, now has every piece:

11
00:00:32,190 --> 00:00:36,017
stock tokens, Chainlink stock feeds, USDG,

12
00:00:36,067 --> 00:00:39,048
and ERC-8004 agent identity.

13
00:00:39,098 --> 00:00:44,905
And Stylus makes solving the strike
on-chain 3.3 times cheaper per proposal.

14
00:00:45,055 --> 00:00:49,517
Each week an agent proposes a
strike, but never touches the funds.

15
00:00:49,567 --> 00:00:52,958
The contract checks it against
the vault's fixed mandate.

16
00:00:53,008 --> 00:00:57,396
On September 29, a reckless
at-the-money put was rejected,

17
00:00:57,446 --> 00:01:01,429
and 10 USDG of its bond
went to depositors.

18
00:01:01,579 --> 00:01:06,073
It is live on testnet: two
vaults, 14 contracts verified,

19
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:11,120
and a buyer agent that
paid 10.01 USDG of premium.

20
00:01:11,270 --> 00:01:14,724
Stonkhouse and Archer Markets
let traders pick strikes.

21
00:01:14,774 --> 00:01:19,297
In Strike, a bonded agent
proposes and the contract checks.

22
00:01:19,447 --> 00:01:24,097
We take 10% of a week's positive
net premium, half to the agent,

23
00:01:24,147 --> 00:01:26,578
and nothing on a losing week.

24
00:01:26,728 --> 00:01:32,417
Behind it: 891 tests and
proofs, 99.3% line coverage,

25
00:01:32,467 --> 00:01:34,710
nine properties proven with Halmos,

26
00:01:34,760 --> 00:01:38,173
and all 11 internal-review findings fixed.

27
00:01:38,223 --> 00:01:40,191
It is not audited yet.

28
00:01:40,341 --> 00:01:44,104
Next: an external audit,
then a capped mainnet vault.

29
00:01:44,154 --> 00:01:48,499
We are asking for a place
at Founder House Singapore,

30
00:01:48,549 --> 00:01:51,626
and introductions to
wallets and market makers.

31
00:01:51,676 --> 00:01:56,492
Try the playground at
strike-options.vercel.app.
